(c) reproduce or create derivative works beyond what is strictly necessary
    for the permitted internal evaluation;
(d) remove or obscure copyright, attribution, or proprietary notices; or
(e) use CVLN names, marks, or logos as an endorsement.

5. SEPARATE COMMERCIAL AUTHORIZATION
Production, deployment, commercial exploitation, redistribution, sublicensing,
and other uses beyond Section 3 require a separate written agreement from the
